  "field": "Computational Biology",
  "summary": "Nathan Sheffield is a computational biologist who develops methods and standards for analyzing genomic region data, particularly chromatin accessibility and DNA methylation. His lab creates infrastructure for reproducible genomics including sample metadata standards (PEP), reference genome management (refgenie), and analysis pipelines (PEPATAC, PEPPRO), with recent emphasis on AI-readiness of biomedical data.",
